55,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"B is software, which is easy to report but adds to board saturation. D has hardware, which complicates audits.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"C and D require field crews or supervisors, which my research shows are very hard to place quickly.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"A and D show the best customer retention. A is software for clinics, which feels very stable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"A and B are software, meaning no physical assets to borrow against, but they won't drain reserves as fast as C or D.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shion,,"A involves medical records, meaning a three-quarter security delay. B is financial, also likely slow. D is hardware—risky.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, if A and B are both slow, is C the fastest? But C has depots, which I know are an audit nightmare.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,C also needs shift supervisors. We can't staff that. I lean toward A or B.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"A serves independent practices, which we know keep their accounts. That warmth and loyalty are precious.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"B is a bridge for merchants. It's clean, but A's market seems more resilient based on Shizue's findings.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shion,,B is the most logical. It avoids the medical security lag of A and the hardware failures of D.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I'm concerned about the board seats for B, but the audit cost of C and D is a dealbreaker for me.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I'll support A. Even with a delay, the staffing is easier than for C or D.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Jonathan. A feels like a gentle, sustainable path.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"A is a good compromise. It's software, so it's easier on the reserves than a warehouse.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shion,,"I still prefer B for the speed of deployment, but if the majority wants A, I can see the logic in the retention.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I will vote for A. The reporting is software-based, and the market is stable.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,A it is.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I am happy with A.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Shion,,"I'll vote B for the timeline, but I suspect I'm outnumbered.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
